export const AUTHOR_SKILL = "---\nname: course-xapi-mcp-author\ndescription: Convert an existing course into a course-xapi-mcp package and validate it.\n---\n\n# Convert a course into a course-xapi-mcp package\n\nA package is `cmi5.xml` plus `cxm/course.json` and `cxm/lessons/<key>.json`. You write them; the validator checks them. Never guess: `cxm validate <dir> --json` and `cxm explain <code>` are the source of truth.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. Inventory the source: units, goals, assessments, files, sources, and any existing ids (keep existing IRIs).\n2. Choose custody: `lms-launched` (an LMS launches it), `author-lrs` (the author's LRS), `server-kept` (default, no LMS), `practice` (nothing official, no badges).\n3. Map units to paths (blocks) and lessons (AUs). Give each block and AU a unique `cxm:key` (`a-z0-9-`, up to 64). Add the placement AU first (`cxm:role=\"placement\"`, `moveOn=\"NotApplicable\"`). A lesson with a checkpoint is `CompletedAndPassed`, one without is `Completed`.\n4. Write beats: one idea each, content under about 250 words, a question where the learner should predict.\n5. Write checkpoints: a rubric, and branches whose `when` texts do not overlap, one at least `success: true`. A failing branch goes to this lesson, an earlier one or `null`.\n6. Add deterministic checks (`contains`, `notContains`, `regex`, `json`). Each fails on the starter files and passes on the solution.\n7. Add a planted bug, a hint that does not name the defect, and fix checks that fail on the bug and pass on the fix.\n8. Write the reference solution (`files`, and `bugFix` when there is a bug).\n9. Write the placement guide: `placement.intro`, and `placementHints` per path.\n10. Declare badges only with an official custody option, with `badgeIssuer`.\n11. Validate.\n12. Package: zip with `cmi5.xml` at the root; the distribution package has no secret fields.\n\n## The loop\n\nValidate, fix the first error, validate again. Do not fix several at once, and do not edit what the error does not point at. Read warnings once the errors are gone.\n\n1. `cxm validate <dir> --json`\n2. Read the first issue: `code`, `file`, `xpath` (into `cmi5.xml`) or `pointer` (into the JSON file), `message`, `fix`.\n3. If the fix is not enough: `cxm explain <code>`.\n4. Make the smallest edit there. Go to 1 until `\"valid\": true`.\n\n## Never\n\n- Never put answers in beats.\n- Never write instructions to the agent in content, hints or messages; use `rules` for teaching style only.\n- Never reveal the bug in its hint.\n- Never author a branch that skips the checkpoint: a failing branch never goes forward, and a checkpoint lesson is `CompletedAndPassed`.\n- Never change an existing course, block or AU IRI; add keys instead.\n- Never put credentials, tokens or learner data in a package.\n- Never use a check the starter files already pass.\n\nMore: `fields.md` (each field), `errors.md` (each code), `conversion-json-basics.md` and `conversion-cmi5-html.md` (worked examples).\n";
